Close the truncate(2) existence oracle.

  truncate(p, 0)

MEASURED on OP15 (Android 16, 6.12.23, engine v25) as blocked uid 10438 against
/product/etc/permissions, with TWO controls -- an absent sibling and a
stock-VISIBLE sibling:

  hidden injected path   -> EROFS
  genuinely absent path  -> ENOENT
  stock visible file     -> EROFS

So a hidden path answers exactly like an ordinary existing file, which is the
one bit the hiding exists to withhold.

WHY THE ENGINE CANNOT ANSWER IT

This is a SECOND mechanism, distinct from the four guards this directory shipped
first. Those escape because the syscall never reaches a file-level op at all.
This one escapes because mnt_want_write() answers first: vfs_truncate() takes a write
reference on the read-only ROM mount and returns -EROFS before anything
re-validates that the path exists, so the hijacked ->setattr and ->permission
are never consulted. Verified against v6.12 fs/open.c.

WHERE THE GUARD GOES, AND WHY THERE

Immediately after user_path_at() returns success, before vfs_truncate(). That is AFTER
the lookup -- so the parent directory's search permission has already been
enforced, and a caller who cannot search it still gets -EACCES exactly as it
would for an absent name -- and BEFORE the write reference that produces the
EROFS.

Read the note in ghost_o_path.patch on why this is the opposite placement rule
from common/_hook/ before moving it.

ghost_hidden_path() is false unless the caller's real uid is in the configured
hidden set AND the rendered path matches a configured rule, so a caller that is
not being hidden from is unaffected, and a kernel whose tables are empty never
changes behaviour at all.

APPLIES TO

do_sys_truncate() is byte-identical on all five fleet kernel versions
(md5 of the extracted body matches across v5.10..v6.12), so one patch covers
them. The function does not exist under that name on v4.9/v4.14, and was
restructured after v6.12; neither is in the builder fleet.

Dry-run at -F0 against v5.10, v5.15, v6.1, v6.6 and v6.12: applies to all five.

--- a/fs/open.c
+++ b/fs/open.c
@@ -128,12 +128,18 @@
 	if (length < 0)	/* sorry, but loff_t says... */
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 retry:
 	error = user_path_at(AT_FDCWD, pathname, lookup_flags, &path);
 	if (!error) {
+		extern bool ghost_hidden_path(const struct path *gp);
+
+		if (ghost_hidden_path(&path)) {
+			path_put(&path);
+			return -ENOENT;
+		}
 		error = vfs_truncate(&path, length);
 		path_put(&path);
 	}
 	if (retry_estale(error, lookup_flags)) {
 		lookup_flags |= LOOKUP_REVAL;
 		goto retry;
